 paradigm</article-title><source>Fam Pract Manag</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11183460</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Avant</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowman</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bucholtz</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Dickinson</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>S3</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><article-title>The Future of Family Medicine: a collaborative project of the family medicine community</article-title><source>Ann Fam Med</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15080220</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Larson</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name><name><surname>Fihn</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirk</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Levinson</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Loge</surname><given-names>RV</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynolds</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>19</volume><issue>1</issue><year>2004</year><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>77</lpage><article-title>The future of general internal medicine. Report and recommendations from the Society of General Internal Medicine (SGIM) Task Force on the Domain of General Internal Medicine</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14748863</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>G</given-